I&#x27;m not so sure, I&#x27;ve made an autobattler and even recently using Astra to come up with new mechanics or cards they&#x27;re usually always bad as if it doesn&#x27;t &quot;get it&quot; even if I feed it all the current cards in game and say &quot;like this, these are good because of x and y.&quot;
When brainstorming, I usually get it to generate 20 ideas and then I come up with something entirely new based on bad stuff it responded with. I&#x27;ve never been able to actually use its ideas verbatim.<p>I&#x27;m not sure if this is a limitation of the tech or whether it will eventually have &quot;taste&quot; in such nebulous domains as &quot;what is fun.&quot; 
They still can&#x27;t write funny jokes despite trillions of dollars of training because even though there&#x27;s plenty of funny material and discussions on what funny is, I guess it&#x27;s still kind of a human thing.
